From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adam Rice <ricea@chromium.org>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 11:29:05 -0700
Subject: Block WebSocketConnector creation in PDF renderer processes

Reject blink.mojom.WebSocketConnector binding requests from PDF-isolated
frames in RenderFrameHostImpl::CreateWebSocketConnector() with
mojo::ReportBadMessage(). A PDF renderer commits the serving origin but
is not permitted to access that origin's data or cookies; allowing it to
create a WebSocketConnector would attach the origin's cookies (including
HttpOnly cookies) to WebSocket handshakes.

Bug: 566683019
Change-Id: I2aecd84c9548c3d1f617b0042808773899a7a19f
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8471069
Reviewed-by: Rakina Zata Amni <rakina@chromium.org>
Commit-Queue: Adam Rice <ricea@chromium.org>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1707308}

diff --git a/content/browser/renderer_host/render_frame_host_impl.cc b/content/browser/renderer_host/render_frame_host_impl.cc
index 4982f8eadf0d3f05c9357f8be44606c4164fadac..5988a4287e251471d625a2ab7aabdf73a2602906 100644
--- a/content/browser/renderer_host/render_frame_host_impl.cc
+++ b/content/browser/renderer_host/render_frame_host_impl.cc
@@ -14938,6 +14938,10 @@ void RenderFrameHostImpl::CreateWebSocketConnector(
     mojo::ReportBadMessage("WebSockets are not allowed in MHTML documents.");
     return;
   }
+  if (GetSiteInstance()->IsPdf()) {
+    mojo::ReportBadMessage("WebSockets are not allowed in PDF documents.");
+    return;
+  }
   mojo::MakeSelfOwnedReceiver(
       std::make_unique<WebSocketConnectorImpl>(
           GlobalRenderFrameHostId(GetProcess()->GetID(), routing_id_),
